      "id": "2on7hts",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Economics"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economics is the social science that studies how individuals, businesses, and governments allocate scarce resources to satisfy unlimited wants.",
        "The four essential factors of production required to create goods and services are Land, Labour, Capital, and Entrepreneurship.",
        "Opportunity cost represents the value of the next best alternative foregone when a choice is made.",
        "Economic activities are broadly classified into Production, Consumption, Exchange, and Distribution.",
        "Scarcity arises because human wants are unlimited while the resources to fulfill them are limited."
      ],
      "id": "q5cx14q"
    },
