    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Adam Smith is known as the Father of Economics; he authored 'An Inquiry into the Nature and Causes of the Wealth of Nations' in 1776.",
        "Factor Rewards: Land earns Rent, Labour earns Wages, Capital earns Interest, and Entrepreneurship earns Profit.",
        "Microeconomics is frequently tested as 'Price Theory', while Macroeconomics is referred to as 'Income and Employment Theory'."
      ],
      "id": "wpoozij"
